  "id": "grid-payload-prf-opening-cribs",
  "status": "published",
  "title": "Page 49–51 payload PRF keys against fixed LP2 openings",
  "question": "Can any pinned B-05 payload-derived key produce one of nine fixed 12-rune known-reading openings at an LP2 page start under the source key-skip rule?",
  "reader_question": "Were the page 49–51 payload-derived keys checked against LP2 openings?",
  "summary": "All 70,680 published B-05 source configurations were checked against nine 12-rune openings at 55 nonempty LP2-00–55 page starts. None produced a complete opening under the source key-skip rule.",
  "finding": "The longest feasible opening was five runes; zero of 70,680 configurations matched all 12. This is a fixed-opening check of already enumerated source keys, separate from the earlier English-score replay.",
  "limitations": "The nine openings and page-start location are assumptions of this test. It does not exclude other plaintexts, other payload-derived constructions, other offsets beyond the source grid, or a general cipher family.",
  "next_steps": "Test a new plaintext or payload construction only when it has an independent reason and a finite, declared scope.",
  "outcome": "not-supported",
